From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: a wineserver that aborts writes its call stack

glibc aborts a process whose heap it finds corrupt ("malloc(): unaligned
tcache chunk detected"); Wine's server turns SIGABRT into exit(1), as it
does SIGTERM, so no core dump is ever written. The machine's server (the
shared Windows system) died that way on a live medium in the s14
regression walk (2026-10-06) and left that one line in the journal --
nothing to find the cause by. Now the server writes "aborted (SIGABRT)"
and its call stack (backtrace_symbols_fd: the binary's offsets, which an
unstripped build of the same version turns into functions) to stderr --
the journal for sg-wineserver.service -- and then ends as before
(exit(1): its atexit work, saving the registry, still runs). backtrace()
is called once at start so its unwinder is not loaded in the handler.

Test: test/srvabort-gate.sh (a scratch prefix's server sent SIGABRT:
"aborted (SIGABRT)" and three or more frames on stderr, exit status 1;
mutant SG_MUTANT_ABORT_SILENT in server/main.c fails it).
---
--- a/server/main.c
+++ b/server/main.c
@@ -29,6 +29,9 @@
 #include <sys/time.h>
 #include <sys/resource.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
+#ifdef __GLIBC__
+#include <execinfo.h>
+#endif
 
 #include "object.h"
 #include "file.h"
@@ -214,6 +217,28 @@
     exit(1);  /* make sure atexit functions get called */
 }
 
+/* Stained Glass OS: the server aborted -- glibc found its heap corrupt
+ * ("malloc(): unaligned tcache chunk detected"), or an assert failed. Wine
+ * ends it as it does a SIGTERM, so no core dump is ever written, and the
+ * machine's server died on a live medium (s14 regression walk, 2026-10-06)
+ * leaving one line in the journal and nothing to find the cause by. Where
+ * it was is written to stderr (the journal) first: the call stack's frames
+ * as the binary's offsets, which an unstripped build of the same version
+ * turns into functions (addr2line). */
+static void sigabrt_handler( int signum )
+{
+#if defined(__GLIBC__) && !defined(SG_MUTANT_ABORT_SILENT)
+    static const char msg[] = "wineserver: aborted (SIGABRT); its call stack:\n";
+    void *frames[64];
+    int count;
+
+    write( 2, msg, sizeof(msg) - 1 );
+    count = backtrace( frames, 64 );
+    backtrace_symbols_fd( frames, count, 2 );
+#endif
+    exit(1);  /* make sure atexit functions get called */
+}
+
 /* Stained Glass OS: the server holds a file descriptor for every file,
  * mapping and socket of every process attached to it. Wine's clients raise
  * their own open-files limit to the hard limit (ntdll's set_max_limit), and a
@@ -247,7 +272,14 @@
     signal( SIGINT, sigterm_handler );
     signal( SIGQUIT, sigterm_handler );
     signal( SIGTERM, sigterm_handler );
-    signal( SIGABRT, sigterm_handler );
+#ifdef __GLIBC__
+    {
+        /* backtrace() loads its unwinder on first use: not in a signal handler */
+        void *frame;
+        backtrace( &frame, 1 );
+    }
+#endif
+    signal( SIGABRT, sigabrt_handler );
 
     sg_init_capabilities();   /* Stained Glass OS: CAP_FOWNER only when needed */
     raise_open_files_limit();
